    "**ADAM ID: **[sm\\_us6000tm81](https://api.adam.geospatial.wfp.org/api/collections/adam.adam_eq_events/items?uid=sm_us6000tm81) Magnitude 6.7 earthquake at 66.665 depth occurred on Aug 20 2026 39km NW of Upahuacho. The epicentre of the earthquake was located at latitude -14.6262 longitude -73.616. It impacted 38505 people within 50km. WFP’s Automated Disaster Analysis and Mapping (ADAM) system is an operational system for collecting, analysing and mapping geospatial and socio-economic information following sudden onset humanitarian emergencies."
